## REAL-WORLD USAGE EXAMPLES

### Example 1: Traditional BOM (Mixed Nuts)
```json
{
  "parentProduct": {
    "nameEn": "Premium Mixed Nuts",
    "productType": "Finished",
    "isManufactured": true,
    "isProcessedProduct": false
  },
  "components": [
    {"productId": 1, "quantity": 50, "unit": "Gram"},
    {"productId": 2, "quantity": 30, "unit": "Gram"},
    {"productId": 3, "quantity": 20, "unit": "Gram"}
  ]
}
```

### Example 2: Process Manufacturing (Pistachio Roasting)
```json
{
  "processType": "Roasting",
  "inputs": [
    {"productId": 10, "quantity": 1000, "unit": "Gram"}
  ],
  "actualOutputs": [
    {"productId": 11, "quantity": 850, "unit": "Gram", "grade": "Premium"},
    {"productId": 12, "quantity": 120, "unit": "Gram", "grade": "Standard"},
    {"productId": 13, "quantity": 25, "unit": "Gram", "grade": "Broken"}
  ],
  "yieldPercentage": 99.5,
  "notes": "Optimal roasting conditions"
}
```

## FRONTEND INTEGRATION GUIDELINES

### Error Prevention (Resolved Issues)
- **Array Handling**: Always ensure API responses return arrays, not objects
- **Type Safety**: Implement proper TypeScript interfaces
- **Null Checks**: Handle undefined/null data gracefully

